Author: Rik Mills <rikmills@kubuntu.org>
Description: Fix crash in kconf_update script for calendar migration
 Upstream detection of the qtpaths binary location at build time finds
 the version/link from the qt6-base dev package instead of the one from
 the qt6-base-dev-tools package. On a user system without the dev package
 the resultant script crashes on not finding the binary at the expected
 path. Instead specificy the path in Ubuntu, which will not change over
 LTS release cycle.

--- a/components/calendar/kconf_update/migrate-calendar-to-plugin-id.py.in
+++ b/components/calendar/kconf_update/migrate-calendar-to-plugin-id.py.in
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
 
 proc = subprocess.Popen(
     [
-        "@QTPATHS_PATH@",
+        "/usr/lib/qt6/bin/qtpaths6",
         "--locate-file",
         "ConfigLocation",
         "plasma-org.kde.plasma.desktop-appletsrc",
